@startuml source-to-deployment
!include theme.iuml
title Test the source that actually exists in the deployed workspace
actor "Module developer" as Dev
participant "Host training checkout" as Training
participant "Host platform checkout" as Platform
participant "Remote training repository" as Origin
participant "Kubernetes init container" as Init
database "Deployed training checkout\nWorkspace PVC" as Deployed
participant "Acceptance tasks" as Tests
Dev -> Training : Preserve WIP; edit on a feature branch
Dev -> Platform : Update setup / deployment when required
alt Published compatible ref; deployed checkout clean
  Platform -> Init : Deploy selected configuration
  Init -> Origin : Fetch published source from origin
  note over Origin,Init
    Init fetches the remote repository,
    not the host checkout's local files.
  end note
  Init -> Deployed : Clone or fast-forward selected ref
else Local changes or deployed WIP
  Dev -> Deployed : Inspect and back up existing changes
  Training -> Deployed : Deliberately synchronize intended files\nor seed an unavailable local branch
  Init -> Deployed : Preserve dirty checkout as script permits
end
Dev -> Deployed : Record actual HEAD and dirty diff
Dev -> Tests : Run applicable module acceptance
Tests -> Deployed : Execute source, kernels and contracts
Tests --> Dev : Logs, executed notebooks, outputs, limitations
Dev -> Training : Commit reviewed training changes
Dev -> Platform : Commit reviewed deployment changes
note over Training,Platform
  Local commits and seeded files are not publication.
  Fresh learners need available source refs and images.
end note
@enduml
